/T (In the UK, the average occupancy rate for all Airbnb properties, including part-time listings, is around 48%. Properties that are managed full-time and achieve less than 50% occupancy are generally considered underperforming. In London, however, the average occupancy rate significantly outperforms the national average, typically ranging between 70-75%, with some central properties peaking at 80% occupancy annually.)
/E (In the UK, the average occupancy rate for all Airbnb properties, including part-time listings, is around 48%. Properties that are managed full-time and achieve less than 50% occupancy are generally considered underperforming. In London, however, the average occupancy rate significantly outperforms the national average, typically ranging between 70-75%, with some central properties peaking at 80% occupancy annually.)
